Adapted sources at that commit:
- src/templates/sheet.js: am-sheet, am-grid, and panel reading order
- src/templates/doc.js: single-column am-doc / am-doc-body structure
- src/templates/panel.js: am-head, panel header, identifier, title, body
- src/themes/index.js: shadcn light-theme variables and system font stacks
- src/themes/base.css: panel, callout, key-value, timeline, and table styling
- src/components/callout.js: semantic note and title/body structure
- src/components/kv.js: definition-list cells and full-row metadata
- src/components/timeline.js: ordered vertical milestones and highlight state
- src/markdown.js: horizontally contained tables and text status indicators

Vetta changes:
- Deliver self-contained HTML in a closed html-preview fence in the main
  assistant conversation; ordinary html fences remain source-first.
- Use inline static CSS, fluid narrow-card layouts (260px / 360px), semantic
  captions/headings, explicit status text, and native details/summary.
- Define theme variables without requiring html data attributes, and preserve
  the content language on body because root attributes may be sanitized away.
- Remove compiler dependencies, custom DSL, CLI/generators, client runtime,
  toolbar/TOC links, external resources, scripts, video/audio, and network use.

This is a curated static presentation adaptation, not the upstream compiler
or a React library. No upstream executable code is bundled or run.
